How do brands reach into our psyches to get us to pull out our wallets at credit cards? What are some of the motivations behind companies that try to appeal to our sense of social responsibility to get us to spend? Our guest for this episode is psychologist Dr. Kit Yarrow, an expert on consulting. Behavior and Professor Emerita at Golden Gate University in San Francisco. She studies why and how people shop and buy and how companies can best meet consumer needs. She's the author of Decoding the New Consumer Mind about the motivations and behaviors of shoppers today and Jen Buy about the consumption habits of millennials. Dr. Yarrow is regularly interviewed on national media, including Good Morning America, NPR and USA Today. Welcome, Dr. Yarrow. It's a pleasure to have you.
